From a855c18b31ccbef1f8855822c5930ac1d9c0c5df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 03:07:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Training-free GT map ablations: derived namespaces and a
 namespace eval launcher

make_ablated_gt_cache.py --mode M rewrites only the grid of a GT namespace
(metadata kept) into <ns>.abl_M[_sSEED]:
  occupancy_only    union of all channels into the 'other' object channel
                    (route-corridor geometry without semantics)
  cell_shuffle      one random cell permutation applied to every channel
                    (category counts and per-cell co-occurrence without
                    geometry)
  regions_only / objects_only
  category_scramble per-episode permutation of object and of region channels
                    (geometry and counts kept, identity destroyed)
  unmentioned_only  complement of mentioned_only (spacy extractor)
The legacy GT generator copies a 7x7 window around every GT path cell and
multiplies unmentioned categories by 0.6, so region channels trace the
route corridor and the value already labels mention; these modes separate
geometry, semantics and mention on the GT-legacy 18600 policy (own 68.41,
nomap 55.68).

eval_gt_namespace.sh TAG NAMESPACE evaluates a PriorGT try5 DAgger ckpt
(CKPT_PATH) on val_unseen with that namespace, optionally with the config
map_ablation modes (MAP_ABLATION), same option set as the other eval
launchers.

